WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday, and I AM TIRED.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.900
I don't mean just physically tired.  Although, I am that.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.600
I mean like metaphysically tired.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.400
I feel like my brain and also my voice are kind of limping to the finish line of 2017

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.400
This is eventually gonna be a happy and celebratory video, but FIRST I have to tell you what's wrong with me.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.539
Some of it is just my mental health problem too much work and travel

00:00:21.539 --> 00:00:27.358
And not enough sleep and exercise are bad for my OCD, but there are also larger forces at work like lately

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:30.700
I feel compelled to scroll through my social media feeds for hours on end

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.700
even though the scrolling generally makes me feel worse.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.100
Because of my mental illness, I've often felt like a passenger in my own consciousness

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.410
with no sovereignty over the thoughts that are called mine and lately

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.030
scrolling through the social internet

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:48.149
I tend to feel like a passenger in the larger consciousness as if history isn't something that we make together

00:00:48.219 --> 00:00:49.829
But instead is something

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:51.400
that's happening to us.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.400
James Joyce called history a "nightmare from which I'm trying to awake"

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.800
and the history unfolding around us these days does often feel like a nightmare to me

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.390
I don't know if this is true for other people

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:04.800
But I often feel powerless in the face of injustice and inequality and violence

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.600
and also social and political structures that don't just Allow for oppression,

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.829
but in some cases actively encourage it.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:15.509
I mean, I'm just one person and I tire easily and I feel like I can't do anything except scroll.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.879
But That is a Lie and this weekend

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.700
I was reminded that it's a lie

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.269
when thousands of people came together from all over the world for the 11th annual project for awesome

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:28.600
which, as I'm recording this, has raised Almost two million dollars for charity.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:33.200
By the way, you can still donate until midnight tonight at projectforawesome.com/donate

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.540
where there are still great perks available.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:40.200
Including New Zealand nickels and project for awesome socks and signed copies of my book Turtles all the way down

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.790
and also at dftba.com you can get this amazing project for awesome t-shirt, all proceeds go to charity.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.700
But whether you participated in the project for awesome by donating or by making a project for awesome video

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:53.159
or by commenting or by joining us in the livestream. Thank you!

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:57.700
Thank you for reminding me that the social internet is not only about passive scrolling.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.600
It's also about hearing stories we wouldn't otherwise hear

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.200
and becoming better informed and making deeper connections with each other.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.200
You reminded me that the social Internet can be a platform for activism and fundraising

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.200
that Truly does make the world suck less

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.200
and along the way you reminded me of something else

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.449
It's not just that we as individuals CAN change the world,

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:20.600
we ARE changing the world, Every day, Each of us through the choices we make.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:24.300
The world isn't somehow separate from our actions and passions and beliefs.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.600
The world is made Out of our actions and passions and beliefs.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.430
During the first half of the project for awesome this year,

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.400
we raised money for two great organizations,

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.400
Save the Children and Last Mile Health.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.800
And the CEO of last mile health, Raj Panjabi,

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.600
who grew up in Liberia, shared with us something his father often told him

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.500
no condition is permanent,

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.629
not the good conditions,

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.000
and not the bad ones.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.700
Inequality of access to health care and educational opportunities are Not Permanent Conditions.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.200
We know this because we've seen dramatic reductions around the world,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.600
but political and social stability also aren't permanent conditions,

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.700
nor is peace or progress.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:02.970
NO condition is permanent and while there are big forces acting upon and within us,

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.600
we are Not mere passengers in history.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.200
The human story isn't something we're scrolling through.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.000
It's something we're part of.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.200
Thanks for reminding me of that.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.200
Hank, I'll see you on Friday

